  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Term that encompasses LGBTQ+ filmmaking, the LGBTQ+ film industry, and film as an art form within LGBTQ+ culture. For specific movies created by or representing LGBTQ+ people, use the term "LGBTQ+ films."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">T&#xE9;rmino que abarca el cine LGBTQ+, la industria cinematogr&#xE1;fica LGBTQ+ y el cine como forma de arte dentro de la cultura LGBTQ+. Para pel&#xED;culas espec&#xED;ficas creadas por personas LGBTQ+ o que las representen, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "pel&#xED;culas LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Term that encompasses lesbian filmmaking, the lesbian film industry, and film as an art form within lesbian culture. For specific movies created by or representing lesbians, use the term "Lesbian films."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">T&#xE9;rmino que abarca el cine l&#xE9;sbico, la industria cinematogr&#xE1;fica l&#xE9;sbica y el cine como forma de arte dentro de la cultura l&#xE9;sbica. Para pel&#xED;culas espec&#xED;ficas creadas por lesbianas o que las representen, util&#xED;cese el t&#xE9;rmino "pel&#xED;culas de lesbianas".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Motion pictures, or movies, created by lesbian directors, depicting lesbians, or that are regarded as important within lesbian culture.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Pel&#xED;culas creadas por directoras lesbianas, que representan a lesbianas o a personas consideradas importantes dentro de la cultura l&#xE9;sbica.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Term that encompasses gay filmmaking, the gay film industry, and film as an art form within gay culture. For specific movies created by or representing gay men, use the term "Gay films."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">T&#xE9;rmino que abarca el cine gay, la industria cinematogr&#xE1;fica gay y el cine como forma de arte dentro de la cultura gay. Para pel&#xED;culas espec&#xED;ficas creadas por o que representan a hombres gay, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "pel&#xED;culas gay".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Motion pictures, or movies, created by gay directors, depicting gay men, or that are regarded as important within gay culture.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Pel&#xED;culas creadas por directores gay, que representan a hombres gay o a personas consideradas importantes dentro de la cultura gay.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Past events or accounts of the past concerning Two-Spirit people, or people who might be perceived as Two-Spirit if they were alive today.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Eventos pasados o relatos del pasado relacionados con personas dos esp&#xED;ritus o con personas que podr&#xED;an ser percibidas como dos esp&#xED;ritus si estuvieran vivas hoy.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people of native African ancestry living outside of the continent of Africa. While this term is commonly used to describe descendants of Africans who were enslaved and forcibly transported to the Americas via the transatlantic slave trade between the 16th and 19th centuries, it can also be used to refer to descendants of Africans who voluntarily immigrated to other parts of the world. Do not conflate with Black LGBTQ+ people or African American LGBTQ+ people. Follow the individual's preference whenever possible.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ de ascendencia africana nativa que viven fuera del continente africano. Si bien este t&#xE9;rmino se utiliza com&#xFA;nmente para describir a quienes descienden de personas africanas que fueron esclavizadas y forzosamente transportadas a Am&#xE9;rica a trav&#xE9;s de la trata transatl&#xE1;ntica de esclavos entre los siglos XVI y XIX, tambi&#xE9;n se puede utilizar para referirse quienes descienden de personas africanas que emigraron voluntariamente a otras partes del mundo. No lo combine ni confunda con personas negras LGBTQ+ o personas afroamericanas LGBTQ+. Siga las preferencias de la persona siempre que sea posible.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Black people who are asexual. Use only for individuals who self-identity as Black. Follow the individual&#x2019;s preference for African American or Black whenever possible.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas negras que son asexuales. Util&#xED;cese &#xFA;nicamente para personas que se autoidentifiquen como negras. Siga la preferencia de la persona sobre el uso de "afroamericanos" o "negros" siempre que sea posible.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Asexual people of African descent born in the United States or asexual people born in African countries who live in or have a strong connection to the United States. Use for individuals who self-identity as African American. Follow the individual&#x2019;s preference for African American or Black whenever possible.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas asexuales de ascendencia africana nacidas en los Estados Unidos o personas asexuales nacidas en pa&#xED;ses africanos que viven o tienen una conexi&#xF3;n fuerte con los Estados Unidos. Util&#xED;cese para personas que se autoidentifiquen como afroamericanas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who were adopted, whether or not by LGBTQ+ parents.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ que fueron adoptadas, ya sea o no por padres LGBTQ+</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who are fathers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ que son padres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bisexual people who are fathers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Obras escritas que incluyan elementos m&#xE1;gicos o fant&#xE1;sticos; util&#xED;cese en referencia a ficci&#xF3;n fant&#xE1;stica centrada en personajes o temas bisexuales.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Gay men who are fathers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hombres gay que son padres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbians who are fathers. This includes non-binary people who have children and identify as fathers, as well as trans women who had children before transitioning and still identify as fathers to those children. Do not use to describe lesbian parents unless they self-identify as fathers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbianas que son padres. Esto incluye a las personas no binarias que tienen hijos y se autoidentifican como padres, as&#xED; como a las mujeres trans que tuvieron hijos antes de transicionar y a&#xFA;n se autoidentifican como padres de esos ni&#xF1;os. No debe utilizarse para describir a padres lesbianos a menos que se autoidentifiquen como padres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Queer people who are fathers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas queer que son padres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who act as a father to one or more LGBTQ+ person. For fathers who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ fathers."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que asumen el rol de padre de personas LGBTQ+. Util&#xED;cese &#xFA;nicamente para describir a personas que se autoidentifiquen como padres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who are mothers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ que son madres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bisexual people who are mothers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Mujeres bisexuales que forman parte de la escena BDSM y asumen el rol de ama en las relaciones sexuales con una din&#xE1;mica ama/esclava.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Gay men who are mothers. This includes trans men who had children before transitioning and still identify as mothers to those children. Do not use to describe gay parents unless they self-identify as mothers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hombres gay que tienen condiciones de salud a largo plazo que requieren atenci&#xF3;n m&#xE9;dica continua y/o impactan o limitan significativamente la vida diaria; algunas, pero no todas, las personas con enfermedades cr&#xF3;nicas se consideran discapacitadas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbians who are mothers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbianas que son madres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Queer people who are mothers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas queer que son madres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who act as a mother to one or more LGBTQ+ person. For mothers who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ mothers."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que act&#xFA;an como madre de una o m&#xE1;s personas LGBTQ+. Para las madres que son LGBTQ+, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "madres LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who have siblings.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ que tienen hermanos.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who share a sibling relationship with one or more LGBTQ+ person. For siblings who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ siblings."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que comparten una relaci&#xF3;n de hermanos con una o m&#xE1;s personas LGBTQ+. Para hermanos que son LGBTQ+, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "hermanos LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who are daughters.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que son hijas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Daughters who have one or more LGBTQ+ parent. For daughters who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ daughters."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hijas que tienen uno o m&#xE1;s padres LGBTQ+. Para las hijas que son LGBTQ+, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "hijas LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who are sons.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que son hijos.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Sons who have one or more LGBTQ+ parent. For sons who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ sons."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hijos que tienen uno o m&#xE1;s padres LGBTQ+. Para los hijos que son LGBTQ+, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "hijos LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who are grandchildren.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ que son nietos.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who have one or more LGBTQ+ grandparent. For grandchildren who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ grandchildren."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que tienen uno o m&#xE1;s abuelos LGBTQ+. Para los nietos que son LGBTQ+, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "nietos LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who are grandparents.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas LGBTQ+ que son abuelos.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who have one or more LGBTQ+ grandchild. For grandparents who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ grandparents."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que tienen uno o m&#xE1;s nietos LGBTQ+. Para los abuelos que son LGBTQ+, utilice el t&#xE9;rmino "abuelos LGBTQ+".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Family members who are LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Miembros de la familia que son LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who have one or more LGBTQ+ family member. For family members who are themselves LGBTQ+, use the term "LGBTQ+ family members."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que tienen uno o m&#xE1;s familiares LGBTQ+. Para miembros de la familia que son LGBTQ+, util&#xED;cese el t&#xE9;rmino "miembros LGBTQ+ de la familia".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbians who have not yet reached the age of adolescence.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Ni&#xF1;as menores de 18 a&#xF1;os que se autoidentifican como lesbianas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Gay people who have not yet reached the age of adolescence.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Ni&#xF1;os menores de 18 a&#xF1;os que se autoidentifican como gay.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who share a romantic, sexual, or play partnership with another person or people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que comparten una relaci&#xF3;n rom&#xE1;ntica, sexual o de juego con otra persona o personas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Individuals who have one ore more romantic, sexual, or play partner who is LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que tienen una o m&#xE1;s parejas rom&#xE1;nticas, sexuales o de juego que sean LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbians who are the romantic, sexual, or play partners of another person or people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbianas que son compa&#xF1;eras rom&#xE1;nticas, sexuales o de juego de otra persona o personas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Gay men who are the romantic, sexual, or play partners of another person or people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hombres gay que son padres.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bisexual people who are the romantic, sexual, or play partners of another person or people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas bisexuales que son miembros de religiones polite&#xED;stas u otras religiones fuera de la cultura dominante que t&#xED;picamente incorporan el culto a la naturaleza y/o lo sagrado femenino, como la Wicca, el druidismo, el paganismo, etc. Util&#xED;cese para describir a las personas bisexuales que se autoidentifican como paganas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Transgender people who are the romantic, sexual, or play partners of another person or people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas transg&#xE9;nero que son parejas rom&#xE1;nticas, sexuales o de juego de otra persona o personas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Queer people who are the romantic, sexual, or play partners of another person or people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas queer que son parejas rom&#xE1;nticas, sexuales o de juego de otra persona o personas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">People who act as parents to one or more people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Personas que act&#xFA;an como padres y/o madres de una o m&#xE1;s personas.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Umbrella term including any of various forms of interactions between police and LGBTQ+ individuals or communities.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">T&#xE9;rmino general que incluye cualquiera de las diversas formas de interacci&#xF3;n entre la polic&#xED;a y personas o comunidades LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A practice in which law enforcement agents or agents of the state coerce an LGBTQ+ person to commit a "crime" they would have otherwise been unlikely or unwilling to commit. Legal definitions of entrapment vary widely depending on the jurisdiction, but the term is often used colloquially to refer to police acting dishonestly or in bad faith, as well as policing focused on anticipating and inducing crime, rather than responding to reports of crime.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Pr&#xE1;ctica mediante la cual la polic&#xED;a induce a personas LGBTQ+ a cometer acciones consideradas delitos que de otro modo no se habr&#xED;an cometido o que era poco probable que se hubieran cometido.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Any of various forms of inappropriate conduct, illegal actions, or abuses of power undertaken by law enforcement agents or agents of the state against LGBTQ+ members of the public. This includes but is not limited to racial, ethnic, and other forms of profiling; unwarranted surveillance, searches, and seizure; selective enforcement; excessive use of force; sexual misconduct; intimidation and witness tampering; falsification of evidence; coerced confessions; false arrests and imprisonment; and bribing or lobbying.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cualquiera de las diversas formas de conducta inapropiada, acciones ilegales o abusos de poder que violentan directa o indirectamente a las personas LGBTQ+, incluidas, entre otras, confesiones forzadas, intimidaci&#xF3;n, arrestos y encarcelamientos falsos, falsificaci&#xF3;n de pruebas, perjurio policial, manipulaci&#xF3;n de testigos, brutalidad y corrupci&#xF3;n policial, elaboraci&#xF3;n de caracterizaciones raciales, &#xE9;tnicos y de otro tipo, vigilancia injustificada, registros o incautaci&#xF3;n de propiedad, soborno o cabildeo para obtener poder o estatus excesivo o para evitar consecuencias, aplicaci&#xF3;n selectiva de la ley y conducta sexual inapropiada.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Any of various forms of inappropriate conduct, illegal actions, or abuses of power undertaken by law enforcement agents or agents of the state against Black LGBTQ+ members of the public. This includes but is not limited to racial, ethnic, and other forms of profiling; unwarranted surveillance, searches, and seizure; selective enforcement; excessive use of force; sexual misconduct; intimidation and witness tampering; falsification of evidence; coerced confessions; false arrests and imprisonment; and bribing or lobbying.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cualquiera de las diversas formas de conducta inapropiada, acciones ilegales o abusos de poder que violentan directa o indirectamente a las personas LGBTQ+ negras, incluidas, entre otras, confesiones forzadas, intimidaci&#xF3;n, arrestos y encarcelamientos falsos, falsificaci&#xF3;n de pruebas, perjurio policial, manipulaci&#xF3;n de testigos, brutalidad y corrupci&#xF3;n policial, elaboraci&#xF3;n de caracterizaciones raciales, &#xE9;tnicos y de otro tipo, vigilancia injustificada, registros o incautaci&#xF3;n de propiedad, soborno o cabildeo para obtener poder o estatus excesivo o para evitar consecuencias, aplicaci&#xF3;n selectiva de la ley y conducta sexual inapropiada.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Any of various forms of inappropriate conduct, illegal actions, or abuses of power undertaken by law enforcement agents or agents of the state against Indigenous LGBTQ+ members of the public. This includes but is not limited to racial, ethnic, and other forms of profiling; unwarranted surveillance, searches, and seizure; selective enforcement; excessive use of force; sexual misconduct; intimidation and witness tampering; falsification of evidence; coerced confessions; false arrests and imprisonment; and bribing or lobbying.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cualquiera de las diversas formas de conducta inapropiada, acciones ilegales o abusos de poder que violentan directa o indirectamente a las personas LGBTQ+ ind&#xED;genas, incluidas, entre otras, confesiones forzadas, intimidaci&#xF3;n, arrestos y encarcelamientos falsos, falsificaci&#xF3;n de pruebas, perjurio policial, manipulaci&#xF3;n de testigos, brutalidad y corrupci&#xF3;n policial, elaboraci&#xF3;n de caracterizaciones raciales, &#xE9;tnicos y de otro tipo, vigilancia injustificada, registros o incautaci&#xF3;n de propiedad, soborno o cabildeo para obtener poder o estatus excesivo o para evitar consecuencias, aplicaci&#xF3;n selectiva de la ley y conducta sexual inapropiada.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Any of various forms of police violence aimed toward LGBTQ+ people.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cualquiera de las diversas formas de violencia policial dirigida hacia personas LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Criminalization of existing or identifying as an LGBTQ+ person, being perceived as LGBTQ+, or engaging in any of various actions considered to be linked to LGBTQ+ status.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">La criminalizaci&#xF3;n de una persona LGBTQ+ por existir o identificarse como tal, ser percibida como LGBTQ+ o participar de cualquiera de las diversas acciones consideradas vinculadas al estatus LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Criminalization of acts considered to be sexual or romantic between individuals perceived as being of the same gender category in a given sociocultural context.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">La criminalizaci&#xF3;n de actos considerados sexuales o rom&#xE1;nticos entre personas percibidas como de la misma categor&#xED;a de g&#xE9;nero en un determinado contexto sociocultural.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unexpected and unannounced entry into and searches of establishments owned or frequented by LGBTQ+ people by law enforcement officers with the aim of using surprise to seize evidence or arrest suspects. Police raids may be undertaken legally using a search warrant or through exigent circumstances, such as probable cause, though the latter is highly subjective and civilians often have little resources to appeal illegal raids.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Un registro no anunciado y sin orden judicial de una residencia o un establecimiento principalmente afiliado o relacionado con comunidades o identidades LGBTQ+ por parte de la polic&#xED;a. Estos ataques suelen ser traum&#xE1;ticos y ca&#xF3;ticos y pueden eludir los procedimientos penales t&#xED;picos y las libertades civiles.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unexpected and unannounced entry into and searches of bathouses, saunas, or spas owned or frequented by LGBTQ+ people by law enforcement officers with the aim of using surprise to seize evidence or arrest suspects. Police raids may be undertaken legally using a search warrant or through exigent circumstances, such as probable cause, though the latter is highly subjective and civilians often have little resources to appeal illegal raids.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Redadas policiales en ba&#xF1;os, saunas, spas, etc. afiliados o relacionados con comunidades o identidades LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unexpected and unannounced entry into and searches of meeting places owned or frequented by LGBTQ+ people, including individuals' residences, businesses, and other institutions, by law enforcement officers with the aim of using surprise to seize evidence or arrest suspects. Police raids may be undertaken legally using a search warrant or through exigent circumstances, such as probable cause, though the latter is highly subjective and civilians often have little resources to appeal illegal raids.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Redadas policiales en lugares de encuentro afiliados o relacionados con comunidades o identidades LGBTQ+, ya sea la residencia de una persona, un negocio u otra instituci&#xF3;n.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unexpected and unannounced entry into and searches of drinking establishments owned or frequented by LGBTQ+ people by law enforcement officers with the aim of using surprise to seize evidence or arrest suspects. Police raids may be undertaken legally using a search warrant or through exigent circumstances, such as probable cause, though the latter is highly subjective and civilians often have little resources to appeal illegal raids.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Redadas policiales en bares afiliados o relacionados con comunidades e identidades LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Unexpected and unannounced entry into and searches of nightclubs owned or frequented by LGBTQ+ people by law enforcement officers with the aim of using surprise to seize evidence or arrest suspects. Police raids may be undertaken legally using a search warrant or through exigent circumstances, such as probable cause, though the latter is highly subjective and civilians often have little resources to appeal illegal raids.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Redadas policiales en clubes nocturnos afiliados o relacionados con comunidades o identidades LGBTQ+</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Primarily Canadian and U.S. American movement wherein police officers were banned from LGBTQ+ pride events in some locations, due to historical and contemporary mistreatment of LGBTQ+ persons, especially Black and Indigenous LGBTQ+ persons. In recent years acted as a response to the 2010-2017 Toronto serial homicides and the mishandling of the investigation by the Toronto Police Service.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Movimiento principalmente canadiense y estadounidense en el que se le prohibi&#xF3; a agentes de polic&#xED;a participar en eventos del orgullo LGBTQ+ en algunos lugares, debido al maltrato hist&#xF3;rico y contempor&#xE1;neo hacia las personas LGBTQ+, especialmente las personas LGBTQ+ negras e ind&#xED;genas. En los &#xFA;ltimos a&#xF1;os, fungi&#xF3; como respuesta a los homicidios en serie de Toronto de 2010-2017 y al mal manejo de la investigaci&#xF3;n por parte del Servicio Policial de Toronto.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Parents who are non-binary.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Padres y/o madres que son no-binarios.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Criminalization of any expression of gender considered to be nonconforming in a given sociocultural context.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">La criminalizaci&#xF3;n de cualquier expresi&#xF3;n de g&#xE9;nero considerada disconforme en un determinado contexto sociocultural.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Criminalization of any expression of gender considered to be cross-dressing in a given sociocultural context.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">La criminalizaci&#xF3;n de cualquier expresi&#xF3;n de g&#xE9;nero considerada transformismo en un determinado contexto sociocultural.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Primarily a U.S. American and Canadian movement which supports divesting funds from, or abolition of, police departments (and often police structures generally) and reallocating them to non-policing forms of public safety and community support, such as social services, youth services, housing, education, healthcare and other community resources.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Principalmente, un movimiento estadounidense y canadiense que apoya la desinversi&#xF3;n de fondos, o la abolici&#xF3;n, de los departamentos de polic&#xED;a (y a menudo de las estructuras policiales en general) y su reasignaci&#xF3;n a formas no policiales de seguridad p&#xFA;blica y apoyo comunitario, como los servicios sociales, los servicios para la juventud, la vivienda, la educaci&#xF3;n, los servicios m&#xE9;dicos y otros recursos comunitarios.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A primarily U.S. American and Canadian political movement that advocates replacing policing with other systems of public safety. Police abolitionists believe that policing, as a system, is inherently flawed and cannot be reformed&#x2014;a view that rejects the ideology of police reformists. While reformists seek to address the ways in which policing occurs, abolitionists seek to transform policing altogether through a process of disbanding, disempowering, and disarming the police. Abolitionists argue that the institution of policing is deeply rooted in a history of white supremacy and settler colonialism and that it is inseparable from a pre-existing racial capitalist order, and thus believe a reformist approach to policing will always fail.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Un movimiento pol&#xED;tico principalmente estadounidense y canadiense que aboga por reemplazar la vigilancia policial con otros sistemas de seguridad p&#xFA;blica. Los abolicionistas policiales creen que la vigilancia policial, como sistema, es inherentemente defectuosa y no puede reformarse, una visi&#xF3;n que rechaza la ideolog&#xED;a de los reformistas policiales. Mientras los reformistas buscan abordar las formas en que se realiza la actividad policial, los abolicionistas buscan transformarla por completo a trav&#xE9;s de un proceso de disoluci&#xF3;n, desempoderamiento y desarme de la polic&#xED;a. Los abolicionistas argumentan que la instituci&#xF3;n policial est&#xE1; profundamente arraigada en una historia de supremac&#xED;a blanca y asentamiento colonial y que es inseparable de un orden capitalista racial preexistente y, por lo tanto, creen que un enfoque reformista de la polic&#xED;a siempre fracasar&#xE1;.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Identification of LGBTQ+ people, or people believed to be LGBTQ+, by police using any of various tools and mechanisms, many of which are pseudoscientific in nature. Such data is then used to entrap and prosecute LGBTQ+ persons, especially in areas where being LGBTQ+ is still criminalized.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Identificaci&#xF3;n de personas LGBTQ+, o personas que se cree que son LGBTQ+, por parte de la polic&#xED;a utilizando cualquiera de diversas herramientas y mecanismos, muchas de los cuales son de naturaleza pseudocient&#xED;fica. Luego, esos datos se utilizan para atrapar y procesar a personas LGBTQ+, especialmente en &#xE1;reas donde ser LGBTQ+ todav&#xED;a est&#xE1; criminalizado.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Identification of LGBTQ+ people, or people believed to be LGBTQ+, by police using digital tools, such as phone records, mobile applications, facial identification algorithms, and artificial intelligence technologies. Such data is then used to entrap and prosecute LGBTQ+ persons, especially in areas where being LGBTQ+ is still criminalized.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Identificaci&#xF3;n de personas LGBTQ+, o personas que se cree que son LGBTQ+, por parte de la polic&#xED;a utilizando herramientas digitales, como registros telef&#xF3;nicos, aplicaciones m&#xF3;viles, algoritmos de identificaci&#xF3;n facial y tecnolog&#xED;as de inteligencia artificial. Luego, esos datos se utilizan para atrapar y procesar a personas LGBTQ+, especialmente en &#xE1;reas donde ser LGBTQ+ a&#xFA;n est&#xE1; criminalizado.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Attitudes and assessments of feelings, relationships, and interactions between LGBTQ+ people and police.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Actitudes y evaluaciones de los sentimientos, relaciones e interacciones entre las personas LGBTQ+ y la polic&#xED;a.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Shooting of LGBTQ+ individuals or individuals perceived as being LGBTQ+ by police officers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Disparos contra personas LGBTQ+ o personas percibidas como LGBTQ+ por agentes de la polic&#xED;a.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ activism undertaken by police organizations and institutions which intends to increase the social capital of such institutions, rather than to actually serve LGBTQ+ communities.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Activismo LGBTQ+ emprendido por organizaciones e instituciones policiales que pretende aumentar el capital social de dichas instituciones, en lugar de servir realmente a las comunidades LGBTQ+.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Historical and contemporary linkages between white supremacist ideologies and modern policing institutions, primarily discussed within the context of the countries of Canada and the United States.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">V&#xED;nculos hist&#xF3;ricos y contempor&#xE1;neos entre las ideolog&#xED;as supremacistas blancas y las instituciones policiales modernas, discutidos principalmente en el contexto de los pa&#xED;ses de Canad&#xE1; y Estados Unidos.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A primarily U.S. American and Canadian decentralized political and social movement advocating for non-violent civil disobedience in protest against incidents of police brutality and all racially motivated violence against Black people. The broader movement and its related organizations typically advocate against police violence towards Black people, as well as for various other policy changes considered to be related to Black liberation.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Un movimiento pol&#xED;tico y social descentralizado principalmente estadounidense y canadiense que aboga por la desobediencia civil no-violenta como protesta contra incidentes de brutalidad policial y toda violencia por motivos raciales contra las personas negras. El movimiento m&#xE1;s amplio y sus respectivas organizaciones suelen abogar contra la violencia policial hacia las personas negras, as&#xED; como a favor de otros cambios de pol&#xED;ticas que se consideran relacionados con la liberaci&#xF3;n negra.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A part of the Black Lives Matter movement which specifically advocates for Black trans people (especially Black trans women) and fights for racial equity and Black liberation.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Una parte del movimiento Black Lives Matter (Las Vidas Negras Importan en ingl&#xE9;s) que aboga espec&#xED;ficamente por las personas trans negras (especialmente las mujeres trans negras) y lucha por la equidad racial y la liberaci&#xF3;n negra.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Works consisting of sequential images often accompanied by text; use in reference to comics focusing on aromantic characters or themes.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Obras que consisten de im&#xE1;genes secuenciales, a menudo acompa&#xF1;adas de texto; util&#xED;cese en referencia a c&#xF3;mics que se centran en personajes o temas arrom&#xE1;nticos.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Literary work, typically written in verse, that focuses on aromantic characters, themes, or identity.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Obras literarias, normalmente escritas en verso, que se centran en personajes, temas o identidades arrom&#xE1;nticas.</subfield>
