  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Primarily used in the United States, this term refers to non-binary people who are not white and who identify as people of color.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Non-binary people of African descent born in the United States or non-binary people born in African countries who live in or have a strong connection to the United States. Use for individuals who self-identity as African American. Follow the individual&#x2019;s preference for African American or Black whenever possible.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Non-binary people of Asian heritage or descent, living in Asia or part of the Asian diaspora. Only use for people who self-identify as Asian.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
