  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Aromantic people who assess, curate, manage, process, preserve, steward, and/or provide access to records and archives of enduring historical value.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Demisexual people who assess, curate, manage, process, preserve, steward, and/or provide access to records and archives of enduring historical value.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Greyromantic people who assess, curate, manage, process, preserve, steward, and/or provide access to records and archives of enduring historical value.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Megasexual people who assess, curate, manage, process, preserve, steward, and/or provide access to records and archives of enduring historical value.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LGBTQ+ people who either study or have expert knowledge in one of the fields of the physical and/or natural sciences, including but not limited to chemists, biologists, physicists, psychologists, and multidisciplinary researchers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Lesbians who either study or have expert knowledge in one of the fields of the physical and/or natural sciences, including but not limited to chemists, biologists, physicists, psychologists, and multidisciplinary researchers.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Gay men who either study or have expert knowledge in one of the fields of the physical and/or natural sciences, including but not limited to chemists, biologists, physicists, psychologists, and multidisciplinary researchers.</subfield>
